&lt;img src="https://we-work-remotely.imgix.net/logos/0171/1153/logo.gif?ixlib=rails-4.0.0&amp;w=50&amp;h=50&amp;dpr=2&amp;fit=fill&amp;auto=compress" /&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
  &lt;strong&gt;Headquarters:&lt;/strong&gt; Toronto, Canada
    &lt;br /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;URL:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://crewvision.io/"&gt;https://crewvision.io/&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;UI/UX Product Designer (Remote – Eastern Europe)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Location&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Remote (Eastern Europe preferred)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Type&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Full-Time Contractor&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Start Date&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As soon as possible&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Compensation&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;$30,000–$37,000 USD/year (paid monthly)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Travel&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Optional 1–2 paid trips/year to Toronto or India&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;About Us&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re building CrewVision, a dispatch and mapping platform for companies that manage snow removal and landscape crews. Our mission is to help growing field service businesses operate like the big guys — without losing the high-margin, high-quality jobs that made them successful.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our product team is based in Toronto, and our full-time developers are in India. Design has been handled by agencies and part-time contributors — now we’re hiring our first full-time, in-house designer to own product design end-to-end.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;What You’ll Own&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a product design ownership role — not a pixel-pushing service gig. You’ll be responsible for everything visual and user-facing in our product:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Collaborate with our product team (wireframes, user needs, problem framing)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Design end-to-end UX: flow, screens, states (error, loading, empty, success)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Handle mobile + web, modals, transitions, and interactions&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Maintain a clean, scalable Figma system (organized files, components, naming)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Manage your own design backlog and roadmap&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Collaborate with devs for accurate, efficient handoff&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reference and migrate legacy Adobe XD files during onboarding&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Spot design gaps, UX friction, or inconsistencies — and propose improvements proactively&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Leverage modern tools and AI to ship faster and smarter&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;What We Value&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe great design is a force multiplier&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We move fast and don’t over-plan — you need to stay useful even when direction is fuzzy&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We like things clean, clear, and fast — and expect you to figure out what matters&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We care more about impact and clarity than Dribbble-style polish&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You don’t need permission to make something better — just show us&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Tools We Use&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Figma (and expect you to set up our full design system)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Adobe XD (for some legacy file reference)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Slack, Zoom, Notion, Loom for async work&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bonus: experience with Framer, Webflow, or AI-enhanced tooling&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Requirements&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;3+ years of experience in UI/UX or Product Design (or equivalent portfolio)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Portfolio that shows real product work — not just visuals&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong English communication (written and spoken)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience collaborating with remote development teams&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Comfortable managing your own design workflow, timeline, and scope&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Familiarity with Adobe XD and Creative Cloud (for migration)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bonus: experience with mapping, dispatch, logistics, or scheduling tools&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;⚠️ No pixel-pushers. We want a partner who can think, own, and deliver — not just someone waiting for tasks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Remote Culture + Travel&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We work across time zones (Toronto, India)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll need 4 hours/day of overlap with Toronto or India&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll have the chance to travel to Toronto or India 1–2 times per year for product strategy or design sprints (we’ll cover travel costs)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;How to Apply&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Send us:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your portfolio&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A short message about a product you helped bring to life&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your location, timezone, and compensation expectations&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bonus: send a Loom video walking through your favorite design decision&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We care more about what you’ve designed than how long you’ve been doing it. If you’ve shipped great product work and know how to explain it, we’d love to talk — even if you don’t check every box.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Our Hiring Process&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We aim to keep our hiring process clear, respectful of your time, and focused on finding a great mutual fit. Here’s what you can expect:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Application Review&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;All applications will be reviewed for relevant experience, portfolio quality, communication, and alignment with the role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Initial Interview&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Selected candidates will have a first-round interview focused on past work, collaboration style, and design thinking.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Paid Test Project&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Finalists will complete a short, real-world design task. This is a paid project and helps us assess execution, process, and attention to detail.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Final Interview&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Candidates who complete the test will be invited to a final interview to discuss product vision, ownership expectations, and long-term fit.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We value clarity, proactivity, and ownership. If that sounds like you, we’re excited to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To apply:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://weworkremotely.com/remote-jobs/crewvision-ui-ux-product-designer"&gt;https://weworkremotely.com/remote-jobs/crewvision-ui-ux-product-designer&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

Apply: https://weworkremotely.com/remote-jobs/crewvision-ui-ux-product-designer

Title: Sansar Tec: Veeva CRM Consultant
Category: Customer Support
Posted: Fri, 22 Aug 2025 07:04:50 +0000
Description:


&lt;p&gt;
  &lt;strong&gt;Headquarters:&lt;/strong&gt; New York, United States
    &lt;br /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;URL:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="http://sansartec.com"&gt;http://sansartec.com&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We are looking for Veeva Consultants with life science and other industries to implement, configure, and optimize Veeva's cloud-based software solutions, primarily focusing on the Vault platform.&amp;nbsp;They act as a bridge between the business requirements of the client and the technical capabilities of Veeva, ensuring successful system implementation and adoption.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;No third parties and W2 only can be considered&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Your responsibilities include, but are not limited to:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Use your extensive knowledge of CRM applications, Salesforce Platform and Veeva CRM suite to define both the high-level architecture and detailed solution design of our applications&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Coach/guide technical design experts and developers on their daily activities, acting as the main technical point of contact for CRM solutions&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Design and implement process to build harmonized global (core) solutions to be deployed in multiple salesforce environments, define core application rules and best practices, solve conflicts between core solutions VS local deployments&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Stay open-minded and curious about new technologies and trends, while making sure that the company is getting the right value from the current and new solutions/technologies being considered for adoption&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Liaise with our partners (software vendors, system integrators, service providers) for the continuous evolution of our solutions, bringing both continuous and disruptive innovations to the table&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Evaluate different data integration patterns and propose/recommend the right solutions for each case&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt; &lt;p&gt;What you’ll bring to the role:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience designing and implementing Veeva-based solutions, in a multi-country / multi-org environment.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience as main solution design / architecture role for CRM implementations&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience on:&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;GDO / CORE models for CRM applications&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Salesforce metadata API or SFDX based deployments, Salesforce metadata packaging, deployment troubleshooting&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Configuring / customizing Veeva CRM software package in Salesforce environments&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Veeva CRM data model, broad knowledge of the different solution areas (MCCP, DCRs, Product Metrics, Consent Management, Approved E-mail, Event Management and other modules)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Working with Pharmaceuticals or Life Sciences is a MUST&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Veeva Certification is a MUST&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Understanding of other Veeva solutions such as Vault (Promomats / Medcomms) and Align&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Very good communication and problem-solving skills; you like to work in agile methodology&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;You have a strong understanding of other related technologies (SQL, SOQL, REST, SOAP, HTML5, JavaScript, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;You have experience with Product Development Lifecycle and DevOps tools like Azure DevOps, GIT, Jenkins, JIRA, etc.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;You can work independently, proactive identify challenges, and be accountable&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To apply:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://weworkremotely.com/remote-jobs/sansar-tec-veeva-crm-consultant-1"&gt;https://weworkremotely.com/remote-jobs/sansar-tec-veeva-crm-consultant-1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

Apply: https://weworkremotely.com/remote-jobs/sansar-tec-veeva-crm-consultant-1

Title: Allegory: Entry-Level Operations Assistant
Category: Design
Posted: Thu, 21 Aug 2025 00:09:11 +0000
Description:


&lt;p&gt;
  &lt;strong&gt;Headquarters:&lt;/strong&gt; New York
    &lt;br /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;URL:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://allegoryclo.com"&gt;https://allegoryclo.com&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Entry-Level Operations Assistant (No Experience Required) – Remote, Full-Time&lt;br&gt;Salary: $700–$900 USD/month to start + performance bonuses&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Location: Remote&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Schedule: Mon–Fri, flexible hours with 2–4 hrs overlap with US time&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;About Allegory&lt;br&gt;Allegory is a clothing brand devoted to storytelling, craft, and culture.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We believe the highest ideal is that of art that inspires. That which exalts the natural feeling. To lift men above their own base nature. That our efforts we can cultivate the artistic state of mind to rise above the common crowd.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Our works begin in humble beginnings. We are simple merchants of apparel, tees, hats, hoodies. Generating 8.5 Million in two years through our efforts of design on these basics, we are expanding into more complex pieces to make our first touch into the world of culture itself.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;In this, we need more team members. Great team members. We need you.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We promote from within.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We need detail-oriented. Cross checking, organized, and hard on the small things.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;If you want a stable, long-term role, this is for you.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;If you want to be apart of a team that aspires to inspire, this is for you.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;If you simply like beautiful design, anime, and art - this is for you.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The Role (We’ll Train You)&lt;br&gt;You’ll start as an Operations Assistant supporting our purchasing, purchase order and invoicing checks, and inventory updates. No prior experience is required. We’ll teach you our process step-by-step. Top performers grow.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;br&gt;Data &amp;amp; Admin: Update spreadsheets, keep records clean, file invoices, and prepare simple reports.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Orders &amp;amp; Inventory: Enter counts, track shipments, flag low stock, and help prevent stockouts.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Quality Checks: Follow simple checklists to verify product details and log issues.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Supplier Support: Send emails, request quotes, and follow up for delivery dates.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Tool Support: Learn the basics of Shopify, ShipStation, and Google Sheets (training provided).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Must-Haves (No Experience Needed)&lt;br&gt;Strong attention to detail—you like getting things 100% right.&lt;br&gt;Comfortable with Google Sheets (basic formulas like SUM/COUNT) or eager to learn fast.&lt;br&gt;Clear written English; professional, friendly tone.&lt;br&gt;Reliable internet and a quiet place to work.&lt;br&gt;Proactive attitude.&lt;br&gt;Ask good questions&lt;br&gt;Follow instructions closely.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Nice-to-Haves (Not required, just a plus)&lt;br&gt;Any exposure to e-commerce tools (Shopify, ShipStation)&lt;br&gt;Experience with basic reporting or admin work&lt;br&gt;Familiarity with purchase orders or logistics&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;What We Offer&lt;br&gt;Competitive starting salary: $700–$900 USD/month (based on skills)&lt;br&gt;Long-term, stable work with a supportive team&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;How to Apply (Fastest Way)&lt;br&gt;Step 1: Complete our Google Form (2–3 minutes). Applications sent via message or email won’t be reviewed.&lt;br&gt;&lt;a class="external_link" href="https://forms.gle/ACH4id3DCPrd8U5e8"&gt;forms.gle/ACH4id3DCPrd8U5e8&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Tip to stand out: In the form, tell us one small system you improved in any past role/school project (even a spreadsheet, checklist, or routine).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To apply:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://weworkremotely.com/remote-jobs/allegory-entry-level-operations-assistant"&gt;https://weworkremotely.com/remote-jobs/allegory-entry-level-operations-assistant&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

Apply: https://weworkremotely.com/remote-jobs/allegory-entry-level-operations-assistant

